description:
In repos/light-dispatch-vessel/src/index.ts, deliver a reach verdict after a dispatch completes, so executions on the autonomous path stop being permanently ungraded.

ANCHOR. The bare line `await postTrace(trace);` occurs TWICE in this file and is therefore ambiguous. Ground instead on this exact three-line sequence, which occurs EXACTLY ONCE:

  await postTrace(trace);

  return {

Insert the new code between `await postTrace(trace);` and `return {`. Do not modify the other `await postTrace(trace);` call site. Do not touch the top of the file or any import.

ONE OPERATION. Compute a boolean named `reachVerdict` and POST it, fire-and-forget:

  const declaredShapes = (tpl.tasks ?? []).flatMap((t) => {
    const os = (t as unknown as Record<string, unknown>)["outputShapes"];
    return Array.isArray(os) ? os.map((s) => String(s)) : [];
  });
  const producedShapes = new Set(outputShapesProduced);
  const reachVerdict = overallStatus === "success" && declaredShapes.length > 0 && declaredShapes.every((s) => producedShapes.has(s));
  try {
    const rctrl = new AbortController();
    const rtimer = setTimeout(() => rctrl.abort(), 5_000);
    void fetch(`${ACTIVITY_API}/v2/activities/execution-traces/reach`, {
      method: "POST",
      headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json", ...auth() },
      body: JSON.stringify({ execution_id: executionId, reached: reachVerdict }),
      signal: rctrl.signal,
    }).catch(() => { /* grading must never fail or slow a dispatch */ }).finally(() => clearTimeout(rtimer));
  } catch { /* verdict delivery is best effort */ }

THE VERDICT SOURCE IS THE POINT OF THIS CHANGE. Do NOT grade `reached: true` on an HTTP 200, and do NOT grade it on `overallStatus === "success"` alone. Either would pump vacuous positive credit into every posterior in the fleet and destroy an honest learning signal; an activity that exits cleanly while producing a wrapper instead of the asked-for output is exactly the hollow completion the reach gate exists to catch. Grade on SHAPE COVERAGE, as written above: reached iff the dispatch succeeded AND every output shape the template's tasks declare actually appears in `outputShapesProduced`. Both values are already in scope at the anchor — `outputShapesProduced` is the accumulator filled from each successful task result, and `tpl` is the template. The local task type may not declare `outputShapes`, which is why it is read defensively above.

WHY THIS IS NOT DEAD CODE. It replicates a delivery block already live in this fleet: `repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/gap-to-feature.ts` posts to this same `/v2/activities/execution-traces/reach` endpoint after a compose, landed in commit c5468ed, currently deployed, and observed delivering verdicts (HTTP 200 at the receiver, and the compose posterior moved as a result). The call is deliberately fire-and-forget with errors swallowed so grading can never fail or slow a dispatch — that is the established pattern in this codebase, not a stub.

MEASURED JUSTIFICATION. Of the newest 3000 execution rows, executions tagged `dispatcher_used:light-dispatch` are graded 0 out of 1072, while goal-host dispatches are graded 46 out of 1370. There is no `execution-traces/reach` call site anywhere in this vessel. Six activities ran 65 executions through this path in one hour and their Thompson posteriors did not move at all.

